# Terraform Backend Configuration (Optional but Recommended for Production)
#
# This enables:
# 1. Remote state storage in Google Cloud Storage
# 2. State locking to prevent concurrent modifications
# 3. Team collaboration with shared state
#
# To enable:
# 1. Create a GCS bucket: gsutil mb gs://your-project-terraform-state
# 2. Uncomment the terraform block below
# 3. Replace 'your-project-terraform-state' with your bucket name
# 4. Run: terraform init -migrate-state

# terraform {
#   backend "gcs" {
#     bucket  = "your-project-terraform-state"
#     prefix  = "spark-cluster/state"
#   }
# }

# Benefits:
# - Prevents "state file locked" errors during team deployments
# - Automatic state backups and versioning
# - Encrypted at rest in GCS
# - No local terraform.tfstate file (safer for secrets)
#
# Learn more: https://www.terraform.io/docs/language/settings/backends/gcs.html
